Sval: the extensions and downloads popovers slide along the screen's edge

Sval's header popovers reach past their button and carry a shadow margin
(sval-header.css). An arrow panel defaults to flip="both" (panel.js), and
where a popover reaches past the screen nsMenuPopupFrame::FlipOrResize
finds no other side to flip to and narrows it to the screen, so its
content is cut off. flip="slide" moves it whole instead
(nsMenuPopupFrame::SlideOrResize), as Firefox's own menu panels do.

diff --git a/browser/components/customizableui/content/panelUI.inc.xhtml b/browser/components/customizableui/content/panelUI.inc.xhtml
index 5c248c0d49..217c7ea41b 100644
--- a/browser/components/customizableui/content/panelUI.inc.xhtml
+++ b/browser/components/customizableui/content/panelUI.inc.xhtml
@@ -68,6 +68,7 @@
          type="arrow"
          noautofocus="true"
          position="bottomright topright"
+         flip="slide"
          hidden="true">
     <panelmultiview mainViewId="unified-extensions-view">
       <panelview id="unified-extensions-view"
diff --git a/browser/components/downloads/content/downloadsPanel.inc.xhtml b/browser/components/downloads/content/downloadsPanel.inc.xhtml
index 5226f65de0..deb6d013d5 100644
--- a/browser/components/downloads/content/downloadsPanel.inc.xhtml
+++ b/browser/components/downloads/content/downloadsPanel.inc.xhtml
@@ -38,6 +38,7 @@
        class="cui-widget-panel panel-no-padding"
        role="group"
        type="arrow"
+       flip="slide"
        orient="vertical"
        hidden="true">
 
